\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textsc  {PyISIS}{} framework architecture showing the five-layer design: (1) USGS ISIS 9.0.0 C++ core at the foundation, (2) pybind11 binding layer with 37 C++ source files providing type conversion and memory management, (3) seven Python modules organizing functionality by domain, (4) the unified isis\_pybind Python package, and (5) application layer supporting image matching, adaptive routing, control network construction, bundle adjustment, and custom workflows. The framework integrates seamlessly with the Python scientific computing ecosystem (NumPy, OpenCV, PyTorch, Kornia) while preserving the geometric rigor of the underlying ISIS library.}}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{5}}
